        "name": "Git setup",
        "kind": "module",
        "responsibility": "Configure global git for SSH signing with the hardware key.",
        "description": "init [--prefer <key.pub> [--title <name>] | --no-prefer]. Writes key.pub and prints it. When gh is on PATH, adds each key that GitHub lacks as a signing key: the machine key as '<host> TPM' or '<host> Secure Enclave', the preferred key as '<comment> via <host> agent' or the --title value. A gh failure prints the gh auth refresh command and init continues. Appends each key for user.email to the allowed signers file, test-signs with the preferred key and reports the result, then sets gpg.format=ssh, gpg.ssh.program, gpg.ssh.allowedSignersFile when unset, user.signingkey=<path to key.pub> and commit.gpgsign=true. When git cannot write the global configuration, it prints the settings as a configuration block.",
